===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Anything that [[pop up|pops up]], ''particularly''
## A pop-up [[advertisement]]; an advertisement that is [[trigger]]ed to appear on a [[computer]] [[screen]] when an [[Internet]] user [[access]]es a particular [[web page]].
## {{lb|en|baseball}} A pop-up [[ball]]: a ball that has been hit to a considerable height above the [[infield]] or the shallow [[outfield]]; a [[pop fly]].
## A folded paper element which [[pops up]] from a book, greeting card, etc.
## A [[business]] that [[quickly]] [[pops up]], such as a [[temporary]] [[restaurant]].
##* {{rfdate|en}} Lonely Planet ''San Francisco Travel Guide''
##*: '''Pop-ups''' often charge restaurant prices, but without advance menus, quality control, health-inspected facilities or professional service. Bring cash and arrive early: most pop-ups don't accept credit cards, and popular dishes run out fast.

